I walk out of my flat.
I reach a large junction.
There are many vehicles there.
But I do not see the bus stop.
There is a small tea shop on the road.
I walk to that tea shop.
A man is making tea there.
I ask him for the way.
"Excuse me, where is the main bus stop?" I ask.
He points his hand to the road ahead.
"Go straight this way," he says.
"There is a large banyan tree there."
I look ahead.
Yes, there is a large tree there.
"From that tree, turn right," he says.
"The bus stop is there."
"Thank you very much," I say.
I walk straight to that tree.
Then, I turn right.
Then I see the bus stop.
